import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const d=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 416 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Quest-Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Ji Ning's Absence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 416 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Quest-Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Ji Ning's Absence","no":416,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Quest Sediment Domain Simulation","Ji Ning Absence","Civilization Collapse","Review"],"related":["08-Quest-Sediment-Domain Simulation Review Plan","85-Copy-Mirror Remote Archaeology Plan","29-Symbiosis Degree Assessment System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0416_模块2-莽荒纪-求索域复盘-纪宁缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md","filePath":"en/0416_模块2-莽荒纪-求索域复盘-纪宁缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md"}`),o={name:"en/0416_模块2-莽荒纪-求索域复盘-纪宁缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md"};function s(r,e,l,c,u,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-416-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilization-collapse-simulation-after-ji-ning-s-absence" tabindex="-1">Entry 416 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Quest-Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Ji Ning&#39;s Absence <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-416-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilization-collapse-simulation-after-ji-ning-s-absence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 416 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Quest-Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Ji Ning&#39;s Absence&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 21) | Benchmark base: Documents 08, 85, 29</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-take-ji-ning-out-of-manghuang-s-world-and-see-what-is-left-of-the-civilization" tabindex="-1">Introduction: take Ji Ning out of Manghuang&#39;s world and see what is left of the civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-take-ji-ning-out-of-manghuang-s-world-and-see-what-is-left-of-the-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: take Ji Ning out of Manghuang&#39;s world and see what is left of the civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the collective ascension axiom requires strong ones not to ascend alone; the causal self-discipline axiom requires eradicating civilizational regression. This entry is Module 2&#39;s fixed action — <strong>Quest-Sediment Domain simulation review</strong>: replicate Manghuang&#39;s world in the Quest Sediment Domain, then &quot;remove&quot; Ji Ning, observe how civilization collapses. This is the most direct experiment to test &quot;protagonist uniqueness dependency.&quot; The law-first axiom reminds: simulation must be based on recomputable law parameters, not imagination. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = high-leaning-medium. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The simulation first reveals a fact: what Ji Ning takes away is not just &quot;a strong one,&quot; but about 40% of the entire civilization&#39;s top-tier combat energy. Once he is absent, the combat balance from Three Realms to Chaos Immortal Realm directly collapses — this 40% energy was never converted into civilization infrastructure, all locked on his person. <strong>The empirical proof of energy waste is the emptiness after absence.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The collapse chain after Ji Ning&#39;s absence (simulation observation):</p><ol><li><strong>Combat vacuum</strong>: Nether Camp remnants, Chaos Immortal Realm old Sovereigns lose suppression; fighting immediately reignites</li><li><strong>Lineage vacuum</strong>: Ji Ning&#39;s lifetime Dao-comprehension goes with him; no later person walks the dual-system peak path</li><li><strong>Affective vacuum</strong>: Yu-Wei line, tribe line lose their guardian; related powers carved up</li><li><strong>Timeline</strong>: about three great-calamity cycles after absence, civilization returns to the starting point of &quot;Great Experts&#39; melee&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The simulation reversely proves: Manghuang civilization&#39;s dependence on Ji Ning is essentially a product of the predation structure —</p><ul><li>Resources all piled on him alone, so he leaves and there is resource vacuum</li><li>Lineage goes with him alone, so he leaves and there is knowledge vacuum</li><li>Order suppressed by him alone, so he leaves and there is order vacuum</li><li><strong>Conclusion: not that Ji Ning is too strong, but that the structure forces him to be strong — this is precisely the predation system&#39;s most eerie self-fulfillment</strong></li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Ji-Ning-Absence Collapse Point</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Anti-Collapse Design</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Combat vacuum</td><td>20% activation strategy: batch middle tier, no single-top dependency</td></tr><tr><td>Lineage vacuum</td><td>Alaya whole-network record; Dao-comprehension perpetual</td></tr><tr><td>Affective/power vacuum</td><td>Anchor Council collective governance; no single guardian</td></tr><tr><td>Back to origin after three calamities</td><td>Law legislation + world backup; civilization stock not lost</td></tr><tr><td>One person leaves and civilization shakes</td><td>Network-style civilization; individual absent does not affect operation</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain fully replicates Manghuang&#39;s sixteen realms, Three Realms—Chaos Immortal Realm resource structure, great-calamity cycle</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;Ji Ning normally in place,&quot; &quot;Ji Ning absent (fallen / ascended not returning),&quot; &quot;Anchor-Symbiosis institutions injected + Ji Ning absent&quot; three controls</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: combat balance, lineage-inheritance rate, post-great-calamity recovery cycle, Myriad-Ranks survival rate</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: after Ji Ning&#39;s absence civilization returns to origin in about three great-calamity cycles; after symbiotic institutions injected, under the same absence civilization does not collapse, and overall energy continuously rises</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-low</strong>. In simulation the &quot;who backfills after absence&quot; rules are vague, all relying on plot</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. If absence were truly written, it would necessarily rely on &quot;new protagonist / new setting&quot; to save the day</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high-leaning-medium</strong>. Simulation empirically — Ji Ning absent gives triple vacuum: combat, lineage, order</li></ul><p>The Quest-Sediment Domain simulation also reveals a counterintuitive conclusion: after Ji Ning&#39;s absence the first to collapse is not combat strength, but who is qualified to argue. Manghuang has no Council; when Ji Ning is present he decides; when he leaves there is not even a place to hold a meeting. Forces can only talk with blades. This shows single-point dependency&#39;s deadliest thing is not losing the strongest, but losing a recognized final arbiter — when rules themselves have no authority, only fists have authority. The meaning of Alaya Network plus Anchor Council is precisely transferring arbitration right from one person to institutions.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: Ji Ning alone locks 40% of top energy; absence becomes emptiness</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: resources, lineage, order all piled on one person; absence = vacuum</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo absent buffered by academy prototype; Ji Ning absent directly triple vacuum</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: after absence Myriad Ranks first crushed in melee</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: a civilization depending on a single protagonist lacks the resilience for cross-plane openness</li></ul><p>The Quest-Sediment Domain simulation also附带 a finding: after Ji Ning&#39;s absence, the first to fill the vacuum is not new strong ones, but the resurgence of old rules. Nether remnants, Chaos Immortal Realm old Sovereigns immediately return to the old road of &quot;fists decide order.&quot; This shows Manghuang&#39;s world fundamentally has no such thing as &quot;order,&quot; only &quot;temporary ceasefire while Ji Ning is present.&quot; Once Ji Ning is taken out, ceasefire ends, war continues. True order should be ceasefire even when no one is present.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Quest-Sediment Domain simulation gives Manghuang its hardest verdict: take Ji Ning out, and this civilization returns to origin in three great-calamity cycles. This is not that Ji Ning is not strong enough, but that the structure makes him alone carry the whole civilization. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s solution is simple — do not let any one person be so strong that when he leaves civilization collapses.</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · Quest-Sediment Domain review · civilization collapse simulation after Ji Ning&#39;s absence described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./415_模块2-莽荒纪-境界体系替代-九境+二境的稳定框架.html">Entry 415 · Realm-System Alternative</a> · <a href="./417_模块2-莽荒纪-制度替代收益-锚点共生注入莽荒世界.html">Entry 417 · Institutional-Alternative Gains</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/85-复制镜异地考古方案.html">85-Copy-Mirror Remote Archaeology Plan</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const g=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{d as __pageData,g as default};
